    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d7-a3">

                <pb facs="1032" n="874" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg874"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Consul Livingston to Vice-Consul Behrmann</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cape Haitien, Haiti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-02-21"><hi rendition="#italic">February 21,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: It becomes my duty to call your attention
                    to the inclosed copy and translation of a communication from the minister of
                    foreign relations of Haiti to the American minister at Port au Prince and
                    referred to this consulate by <pb facs="1033" n="875" xml:id="pg875"/> the
                    American minister, making charges of political activity on your part against the
                    present Haitian Government and withdrawing your exequatur.</p>
                <p>You are requested to make reply to these charges without delay and forward the
                    same to this consulate.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lemuel W.
                    Livingston.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
